 is such a good shout!  I was at the Gtech yesterday, checking out Sangare, Ajer and Thiago.  Schade is sharp and certainly ahead of Anthony right now (cant believe I actually forgotten him; something to seriously consider in my no Haaland BB1 draft, especially he has great fixture in my potential weakest GW3, and more affordable than Thiago, since I already have Isak - my GW3 captain, and Pedro must have for GW4).  I try not to be biased but as the Bees supporter I plan to attend more games this season, coz we finally feel like a proper UEFA level side now.  Sangare is more box-to-box than defensive midfielder, and has this classy touch/control like Toney/Wissa, and already in a position to one touch pass or dribble before he receive the ball -  think he will proved to be the difference in our midfield when there would be less time and space in the actual competitive games (his attacking threat on open play + defcon should outscore Gross\u0027s occasional set-piece with minutes risk)","author":{"@type":"https://schema.org/Person","name":"@repentmaster2842","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@repentmaster2842","alternateName":"Repent Master"},"upvoteCount":25}]}</script><script nonce="yaOxIU7G-hFuOEeoW6_7wg">if (window.ytcsi) {window.ytcsi.tick('bc', null, '');}var ytimg={count:0,preload:function(src){var img=new Image;var count=++ytimg.count;ytimg[count]=img;img.onload=img.onerror=function(){delete ytimg[count]};img.src=src}};
